Let me first understand the vulnerability more precisely. The key issue is in `initialize_context_decompression`:

```c
if ((context->header_flags & BLOSC_DOSHUFFLE) &&
    (context->header_flags & BLOSC_DOBITSHUFFLE)) {
    /* Extended header */
    ...
    int max_filters = (header_version == BLOSC2_VERSION_FORMAT_ALPHA) ? 5 : BLOSC2_MAX_FILTERS;
    for (int i = 0; i < max_filters; i++) {
      context->filters[i] = filters[i];
      context->filters_meta[i] = filters_meta[i];
    }
    ...
}
```

When `header_version == 3` (alpha), `max_filters = 5`, so `context->filters[5]` and `context->filters_meta[5]` are NOT initialized. Then in `blosc_d`, `last_filter(filters, 'd')` reads `filters[5]` (uninitialized).

Now, the `context` is a global context (`g_global_context`) in the fuzzer path (since `blosc2_decompress` uses `g_global_context` when `BLOSC_NOLOCK` is not set). The context is created once. So the uninitialized value in `filters[5]` depends on the initial state of the context.

